{
  "$comment": "Sprite sheet animations. A sheet is one PNG with `frames` equal-width frames side by side (frame width = PNG width / frames). Sprites not listed here are single images. mode \"time\" (default): plays at `fps`; loop=false stops on the last frame. mode \"velocity\": the jump phase picks the frame \u2014 the rising frames spread over the way up (first = take-off), the LAST frame is for landing and going down (no fps/loop). sourceFrames: which frames of the source strip (assets/sprite-sources) the generator keeps. Pixel density is fixed: 128 px of frame height = 1 tile, so a bigger frame is drawn bigger (anchored at the bottom centre). surfaceY (platforms): px from the top of the frame down to the walkable surface (default 0), so drawn art such as grass tufts can stick up above it.",
